<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Plan of Tuxtepec</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1876">1876</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Plan of Tuxtepec was the revolt proclaimed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/porfirio-diaz">Porfirio Díaz</a> in January 1876 against President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sebastian-lerdo-de-tejada">Sebastián Lerdo de Tejada</a>'s bid for re-election, under the banner of no re-election. After his victory at Tecoac in November 1876 Díaz took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico-city">Mexico City</a> and became president, beginning the long period of his rule known as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/porfiriato">Porfiriato</a>.</p></div>
